WHAT TO JUDGE — three questions, in order
1. Does EVERY clause of the criterion have a row, or a stated reason it has
   none? An empty cell is the finding, not an omission you should excuse.
2. Can each named row actually FAIL? Specifically: is there a fixture that
   makes its own assertion true, a staging step that removes the condition the
   row observes, or an assertion so weak that the mutant it names would still
   pass? Name the row and the mechanism.
3. Did any round-1 repair introduce a new defect, or leave the original finding
   still stateable in different words?

Be adversarial. A finding is a lead until verified at source — cite file:line
